#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:194
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For displaying mail, <application>mailx</application> uses a pager program. "
"Since the default of <command>pg</command> is not available on a LFS system,"
" you need to specify which pager <command>mailx</command> is supposed to "
"use. By default, the <command>more</command> and the more comfortable "
"<command>less</command> commands are installed. If the <envar>PAGER</envar> "
"environment variable is not set in <filename>/etc/profile</filename> or "
"<filename>~/.bash_profile</filename>, or if it should be set to another "
"pager specifically for reading mails, it can be set system wide in "
"<filename>/etc/nail.rc</filename> as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""
"Para exibir mensagens, o <application>mailx</application> usa um programa "
"paginador. Como o padrão <command>pg</command> não está disponível em um "
"sistema LFS, você precisa especificar qual paginador é presumido que "
"<command>mailx</command> use. Por padrão, o <command>more</command> e o mais"
" confortável <command>less</command> estão instalados. Se a variável de "
"ambiente <envar>PAGER</envar> não estiver configurada em "
"<filename>/etc/profile</filename> ou em "
"<filename>~/.bash_profile</filename>, ou se ela deveria estar configurada "
"para outro paginador especificamente para leitura de mensagens, ela pode ser"
" configurada abrangente a todo o sistema em "
"<filename>/etc/nail.rc</filename>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:207
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo \"set PAGER=<replaceable>&lt;more|less&gt;</replaceable>\" "
"&gt;&gt; /etc/nail.rc</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>echo \"set PAGER=<replaceable>&lt;more|less&gt;</replaceable>\" "
"&gt;&gt; /etc/nail.rc</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:209
#, xml-text
msgid "or for the current user in <filename>~/.mailrc</filename>:"
msgstr "ou para o(a) usuário(a) atual em <filename>~/.mailrc</filename>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:211
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo \"set PAGER=<replaceable>&lt;more|less&gt;</replaceable>\" "
"&gt;&gt; ~/.mailrc</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>echo \"set PAGER=<replaceable>&lt;more|less&gt;</replaceable>\" "
"&gt;&gt; ~/.mailrc</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:214
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Other interesting options to set in the config files might be EDITOR and "
"MAILDIR."
msgstr ""
"Outras opções interessantes para configurar nos arquivos de configuração "
"podem ser &quot;EDITOR&quot; e &quot;MAILDIR&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:219
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If the default editor is not set in the environment for other packages, it "
"can be set by running the following command as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""
"Se o editor padrão não estiver configurado no ambiente para outros pacotes, "
"ele poderá ser configurado executando-se o seguinte comando como o(a) "
"usuário(a) &root;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:223
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo \"set "
"EDITOR=<replaceable>&lt;vim|nano|...&gt;</replaceable>\" &gt;&gt; "
"/etc/nail.rc</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>echo \"set "
"EDITOR=<replaceable>&lt;vim|nano|...&gt;</replaceable>\" &gt;&gt; "
"/etc/nail.rc</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:226
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Depending on which kind of <xref linkend=\"server-mail\"/> is installed, it "
"might be necessary to set the MAILDIR variable so that "
"<application>mailx</application> is able to find mail as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""
"Dependendo de qual tipo de <xref linkend=\"server-mail\"/> esteja instalado,"
" pode ser necessário configurar a variável MAILDIR, de maneira que "
"<application>mailx</application> esteja apto a encontrar mensagens. Como o "
"usuário &root;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:232
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>echo \"set MAILDIR=Maildir\" &gt;&gt; /etc/nail.rc</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>echo \"set MAILDIR=Maildir\" &gt;&gt; /etc/nail.rc</userinput>"

